---

This application bundles third-party code. The dependency tree is 666 crates
plus the npm packages listed in package.json, and every one of them is under a
permissive licence — overwhelmingly MIT or Apache-2.0, which this licence is
compatible with.

Three groups are worth naming because they ask for something beyond the notice
above:

  * MPL-2.0 (attohttpc, cssparser, cssparser-macros, dtoa-short, option-ext,
    selectors). File-level copyleft: these crates are used unmodified and are
    linked, not altered, so the obligation is to say they are here and to point
    at their sources, which their crates.io pages do. Modifying one of those
    files would mean publishing that file's changes.

  * Unicode-3.0 (icu_collections and the rest of the ICU4X crates, plus part of
    unicode-ident). Requires the Unicode licence notice to travel with
    distributions that include the data.

  * Apache-2.0 crates require their NOTICE files, where present, to be carried
    along. The Apache-2.0 text is at https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0

The application also downloads, at the user's request and onto their own
machine, software this project does not distribute: Eclipse Temurin JDKs from
Adoptium (GPLv2 with Classpath Exception), Minecraft server jars from Mojang
(under Mojang's own EULA, which the user accepts per server), and mods and
modpacks from Modrinth and CurseForge under their authors' licences. None of
that is bundled here.
